    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 81.88 efficiency score. His matchup against Melton is prime; a 16% park factor boost combined with an 8% lineup placement advantage creates a high-ceiling environment for both counting stats and potential stolen bases. While we are also leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** (70.48) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.00), **Gunnar Henderson** is the primary driver of our daily projection. **Jackson Merrill** (61.54) rounds out our strong starts, benefiting from a favorable 13% platoon edge against Medina, which helps mitigate a slightly tougher opposing SP_xERA of 3.98.\n\nOur depth remains tested by the lengthy injury report featuring **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco**, which forced a difficult decision regarding the bench. **Nasim Nunez** (55.68) narrowly edged out internal utility options to secure the final spot; his 11% boost from the SP skill profile and an favorable matchup against the left-handed P\u00e9rez helped him clear the marginal threshold, whereas players like **Coby Mayo** and **Nolan Schanuel** remain on the outside looking in due to less optimal platoon splits today. While **Liam Hicks** (51.54) and **Miguel Vargas** (55.29) hover in the marginal tier, their leadoff and three-hole slots respectively provide just enough volume to justify their inclusion over deeper reserves like **Heliot Ramos** or **Jacob Wilson**, whose current lineup positions limit their projected output. We will continue to monitor the weather reports for any late-breaking changes that could impact the efficiency of **Andy Pages** (57.97) against Sproat, as any shift in wind patterns could necessitate a rotation to protect our games-played caps.",
